      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 7 - Sing a MIDI file\n\nA tune you already have as MIDI, sung by YuE2 in the style you describe.\n**YuE2 Load MIDI** reads the file and writes its melody as a score, and\n**YuE2 Generate Song** lays the words written on it along that tune and sings\nthem.\n\n## What it needs\n\nThe YuE2-3B weights, 7.26 GB, downloaded on the first run. Nothing is\ndownloaded for the MIDI file: it is read on the spot.\n\n## Before pressing Run\n\n1. **Choose the file.** Press **Choose MIDI file...** on *The MIDI file*, or\n   drop a `.mid`, `.midi`, `.kar` or `.rmi` file on that node. The list under\n   the button names the file's tracks and shows which one the voice takes.\n2. **Check the voice.** If `auto` took the wrong track, set **vocal_track** to\n   the number of the tune in that list. Drums are never sung, and a track\n   that plays chords is sung as its top note.\n3. **Write the style and the words** on *Sing it*. The file gives the tune,\n   the words are yours.\n\n## How the words meet the tune\n\nA MIDI file has a tune and no words, so *Sing it* lays yours along it: each\nline on a phrase with about as many notes as the line has syllables. A riff\nwith no room for a line is passed over, the tune comes round again when the\nwords outlast it, a chorus sung twice gets the same bars, and the song ends\none bar after the last line. The node says which bars each section is sung on.\n\nWords come out clearly when the tune has room for them: a line of seven\nsyllables wants a phrase of about seven notes with a breath after it. Over a\nfast theme with twice the notes and no breaths, YuE2 tends to sing sounds or\nwords of its own however the lines are laid, and the node warns with the\nnumbers.\n\nFor a karaoke file sung with its own words, turn **without_sections** off on\n*The MIDI file* and wire its **lyrics** into *Sing it*: the score keeps the\nfile's own sections and is sung as it is.\n\n## Why cot is melody\n\n**cot** in *Settings* is `melody`: the score gives the tune, and the style\nline decides the accompaniment. Set **mode** on *The MIDI file* and **cot**\nhere to `full` together to have chords guessed from the file's other tracks\nas well.\n\n## Length\n\nThe song ends with the words. At `0`, **max_seconds** still caps it at about\n12 seconds a sung line; the score editor draws the line where the song ends.\n\n## Next\n\n**Edit score...** on *The MIDI file* opens the tune on a piano roll, and an\nedit is kept for this file. **Save as MIDI...** in that window saves the\nedited score back as a MIDI file."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# 7 - Sing a MIDI file\n\nA tune you already have as MIDI, sung by YuE2 in the style you describe.\n**YuE2 Load MIDI** reads the file and writes its melody as a score, and\n**YuE2 Generate Song** sings that score with the words written on it.\n\n## What it needs\n\nThe YuE2-3B weights, 7.26 GB, downloaded on the first run. Nothing is\ndownloaded for the MIDI file: it is read on the spot.\n\n## Before pressing Run\n\n1. **Choose the file.** Press **Choose MIDI file...** on *The MIDI file*, or\n   drop a `.mid`, `.midi`, `.kar` or `.rmi` file on that node. The list under\n   the button names the file's tracks and shows which one the voice takes.\n2. **Check the voice.** If `auto` took the wrong track, set **vocal_track** to\n   the number of the tune in that list. Drums are never sung, and a track\n   that plays chords is sung as its top note.\n3. **Write the style and the words** on *Sing it*. The file gives the tune,\n   the words are yours. For a karaoke file, wire **lyrics** from *The MIDI\n   file* into *Sing it* instead, and the file's own words are sung.\n\n## Why cot is melody\n\n**cot** in *Settings* is `melody`: the score gives the tune, and the style\nline decides the accompaniment. Set **mode** on *The MIDI file* and **cot**\nhere to `full` together to have chords guessed from the file's other tracks\nas well.\n\n## Length\n\nThe singing stops at **max_seconds**. At `0` the ceiling comes from the\nwords, 12 seconds a sung line, so a long file with few lines is cut short;\nthe score editor draws the line where the song ends. Raise **max_seconds** or\nwrite more lines.\n\n## Next\n\n**Edit score...** on *The MIDI file* opens the tune on a piano roll, and an\nedit is kept for this file. **Save as MIDI...** in that window saves the\nedited score back as a MIDI file."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
